exit: 1
--- stdout
{
  "refused": [
    "SENSOR_IP is set but empty; accepted: the sensor's own IPv4 address, for example 192.168.20.20",
    "SENSOR_ID is set but empty; accepted: a lowercase letter then up to 30 lowercase letters, digits or single '_', or unset it for the default",
    "DATA_PORT is set but empty; accepted: a UDP port 1024-65535 (default 4444), or unset it for the default",
    "FRAME_ID is set but empty; accepted: letters, digits and '_', not starting with a digit (default voyant_sensor), or unset it for the default"
  ]
}
--- stderr
voyant-driver: refusing to start: SENSOR_IP is set but empty; accepted: the sensor's own IPv4 address, for example 192.168.20.20
voyant-driver: refusing to start: SENSOR_ID is set but empty; accepted: a lowercase letter then up to 30 lowercase letters, digits or single '_', or unset it for the default
voyant-driver: refusing to start: DATA_PORT is set but empty; accepted: a UDP port 1024-65535 (default 4444), or unset it for the default
voyant-driver: refusing to start: FRAME_ID is set but empty; accepted: letters, digits and '_', not starting with a digit (default voyant_sensor), or unset it for the default
